              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "peregrīnor, peregrīnārī — \"to travel abroad, to live in foreign parts\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Mercātor multōs annōs in terrīs longinquīs peregrīnātur. The merchant travels abroad in distant lands for many years."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Deponent: peregrīnor, peregrīnārī, peregrīnātus sum. English pilgrim comes from the related adjective peregrīnus."
            }
          ]
        },
